## Event Registration Automation

## Project Overview
This is an automated event registration workflow built with Zapier and Google Forms to simplify the registration process, streamline information collection and reduce repetitive administrative tasks.

## Problem Statement
Managing event registrations manually can be time-consuming and inefficient. Collecting participant information, organising submissions and carrying out repetitive administrative activities can create unnecessary workload.
This automation was designed to simplify the process and improve registration management.

## Objectives
Automate the event registration process.
Streamline the collection of participant information.
Reduce repetitive administrative tasks.
Improve the efficiency of registration management.

## Tools and Technologies
Zapier
Google Forms
Google Sheets
Gmail

## Workflow Overview
The automation begins when a participant submits an event registration form through Google Forms. Then, Zapier detects the new submission and triggers the configured actions to process the registration information.

**Trigger:** New Google Forms submission.

**Actions:**
I use formatter by Zapier to capitalize attendees names.
The details in the form is then recorded on a spreadsheet.
Filter by Zapier is an action that allows the Zap to continue only if Email Address and Number of Tickets are included in the Google Sheet.
Then the attendees receive an email to notify of successful submission and that they will be sent a reminder for the event soon.
A delay action stops the zap from moving forward by delaying until a set day and time so all attendees get a reminder email at the same time.
The reminder email is sent at the right time.

## Business Value
- Reduces manual administrative workload.
- Streamlines participant information collection.
